{"id": "EUVD-2026-104535", "enisaUuid": "66147294-e5db-3e52-8751-2d96af123b0d", "description": "CCC Attestation SIG attested-tls-poc through commit 731ca82 fails to bind early attestation Evidence to the TLS connection, allowing attackers to relay valid Evidence from a genuine attester. Attackers holding an extracted attested TLS private key can forward the relying party's nonce to a genuine attester and replay its Evidence to impersonate the attested workload and intercept data.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T17:26:39", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T17:39:42", "baseScore": 9.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/CCC-Attestation/attested-tls-poc/pull/58", "https://github.com/CCC-Attestation/attested-tls-poc/tree/5b6c5374b3fe8b671906c8ab32f6134d9c3da26d/relay-attacks-formal", "https://github.com/ionut-arm/mbedtls/blob/f4ac7593826a506fc509c83cad73786acab1d442/library/ssl_tls13_generic.c#L430-L436", "https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-intra-handshake-fail/", "https://github.com/muhammad-usama-sardar/intra-handshake.fail", "https://github.com/CCC-Attestation/attested-tls-poc", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ccc-attestation-sig-attested-tls-poc-through-commit-731ca82-attestation-relay-attack"], "aliases": ["GHSA-hqrh-qq2r-6h96", "CVE-2026-112377"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "75a8c21f-9063-363b-8d89-01ca81a3a70c", "product": {"name": "attested-tls-poc", "vendor": {"name": "CCC-Attestation"}}, "product_version": "0 \u2264731ca82ed533fc7a1092be980887ae2e34261da2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "d3f17df3-3db0-3a90-82f9-4d7a0b46bf32", "vendor": {"name": "CCC-Attestation"}}], "isExploited": false}